1. The following projects have been approved under the national health grants program to provide federal assistance to crippled children in the province of Quebec:
Assistance toward extending the services of -the orthopaedic section of the hopital du Sacre-Coeur, Cartierville;
Assistance toward extending the services of l'Ecole Cardinal Villeneuve, Quebec City;
The provision of large quantities of orthopaedic appliances to be supplied to crippled children through a number of orthopaedic centres;
Assistance toward extending the services of La Societe de Secours aux Enfants Infirmes, Montreal;
Employment of supplementary staff to extend the services of the speech therapy clinic of the Royal Victoria hospital, Montreal;

Questions
Provision of staff and equipment for the Rehabilitation Society for Cripples, Montreal;
Assistance toward extending the services of the Orthopaedic Centre of La Societe de Rehabilitation, Inc., Sherbrooke.
